					</td>
				</tr>
				<tr>
					<td>Angled corner cut</td>
					<td>10px</td>
					<td>--button-cut-size</td>
					<td>Private candidate</td>
					<td>
						Propose button-owned --_cut-size: 10px while this geometry is
						specific to buttons. Promote a shared cut-size only when multiple
						surface types intentionally share that shape contract.
					</td>
				</tr>
				<tr>
					<td>Secondary / primary minimum width</td>
					<td>120px / 172px</td>
					<td>Study literals</td>
					<td>Private candidate</td>
					<td>
						Propose --_min-width: 120px and a filled-variant override of 172px
						if these composition constraints are retained. Remove them if
						content should determine width. Do not add generic control widths
						without shared use.
					</td>
				</tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
